-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",22,{
[673]="70022D6B\n1\tBring the letter to Tralli in Bree\tTralli sent you a letter requesting that you visit him near the Bree Jail. Deliver the letter to Tralli. He can be found near the Bree Jail.\n",
[674]="70022D6D\n1\tBring the letter to Biarn in Bree\tBiarn sent you a letter requesting that you visit him at the Scholar's Stair in Bree. Deliver the letter to Biarn within the Scholar's Stair in Bree.\n",
[675]="70022D70\n1\tBring the letter to Flambard Took in Bree\tFlambard Took sent you a letter requesting that you visit him in Bree. Deliver the letter to Flambard Took. He can be found near the Hunting Lodge in Bree.\n",
[676]="70022D74\n1\tBring the letter to Oggur in Bree\tOggur sent you a letter requesting that you visit him in the Bree Jail. Deliver the letter to Oggur. He can be found in the Bree Jail.\n",
[677]="70022D7F\n1\tBring the letter to Daisy Appledore in Bree\tDaisy Appledore sent you a letter requesting that you visit her at Bree Jail. Deliver the letter to Daisy Appledore within the Bree Jail.\n",
[678]="700586C5\n1\tBring the letter to Brom Hawksbeard in the Bree Jail\tBrom Hawksbeard sent you a letter requesting that you visit him in the Bree Jail. Deliver the letter to Brom. He can be found in the Bree Jail.\n",
[679]="70064233\n1\tBring the letter to Barliman Butterbur in the Prancing Pony\tBarliman Butterbur sent you a letter requesting that you visit him in the Prancing Pony. Deliver the letter to Barliman Butterbur. He can be found in the Prancing Pony in Bree-town.\n",
[680]="70016716\n1\tCollect the \"other orders\"\tWhite Hand guards can be found in the Redhorn Lodes amongst the buildings called the Ore-house, Menem-mezel, and Malmezel, south-east of the Orc-watch. Ingifast wants you to find out about the \"other orders\" the White Hand may be carrying. He suggested you start with the White Hand guards in the Redhorn Lodes.\n2\tCollect the \"other orders\"\tWhite Hand guards can be found in the Redhorn Lodes amongst the buildings called the Ore-house, Menem-mezel, and Malmezel, south-east of the Orc-watch. Ingifast wants you to find out about the \"other orders\" the White Hand may be carrying. He suggested you start with the White Hand guards in the Redhorn Lodes.\n3\tBring the \"other orders\" to Ingifast in the Orc-watch\tIngifast is at the Orc-watch, north-west of the Ore-house, Menem-mezel, and Malmezel. Ingifast will be interested in seeing the copy of the \"other orders\" you managed to obtain.\n",
[681]="70032C23\n1\tWhite Hand raiding parties can be found on the cleared path between the two tribes of Orcs. Ingifast wants you to find a raiding party of the White Hand and dispatch them.\t\n2\tReturn to Ingifast\tIngifast is camped on the stairs leading up to the Orc-watch. You should return to Ingifast with news of your success.\n",
[682]="70067CB1\n1\tCollect Methen's debt\030Collect Akubis's debt\030Collect Yigo's debt\030Collect Dagan's debt\tIthurga wants you to collect debts from residents holding back their tithes. He directed you to scout the town for Methen, Akubis, Dagan, and Yigo to collect their debts.\n2\tDeliver the debts to Ithurga\030Collect Collected Debt (total: 4)\tYou collected the four debts. Return to Ithurga at his abode in lower Halrax.\n3\tBring your tithe to Ithurga\030Collect a bag of gold coins\tIthurga directed you to purchase a bag of coins that matter to him from the vault-keeper in Halrax. The vault is in the upper ward of the township. Return to Ithurga with your tithe.\n",
[683]="700272C0\n1\tPlace the desecrated ox-skull before the tent of the Ox-clan's captain\tThe Ox-clan captain's tent may be found within Rhuvel-cadlus, in the valley below Cuthric's post. Cuthric wants you to place a desecrated ox-skull before the tent of the Ox-clan's captain in an effort to goad him into single combat.\n2\tTalk to Cuthric\tCuthric is hiding on the ridge above Rhuvel-cadlus. You should return to Cuthric and tell him that you have done as he asked.\n",
[684]="7002C5B7\n1\tUse the rope to bring Dargum before the leaders of Stangard\tThe Uruk-hai Dargum may be bound using the coil of strong rope near his tent along the river in the southern Wailing Hills. Odda has asked you to take the Uruk before Stanric if you could manage to capture him alive.\n2\tTalk to Byrnstan in Stangard\tByrnstan can be found on duty in Stangard, outside the Mead Hall. Gadda is displeased with the command to release Dargum and has asked Byrnstan to express his concerns to you.\n",
[685]="70007019\n1\tTalk to Medium Armoursmith\030Collect Armour for Trestlebridge\tJarred Mason is an armourer in Trestlebridge, far to the west and south of Esteldín, along the Greenway. Gondranc completed the armour he had promised for the people of Trestlebridge and has only to deliver it. He has asked you to act as his courier and deliver the armour to a man named Jarred Mason.\n2\tTalk to Gondranc\tGondranc resides at Esteldín, far to the north and east of Trestlebridge. Jarred Mason has asked you to return to Gondranc with his thanks for the armour.\n",
[686]="7006C6FC\n1\tComplete the Instance: A Promise Kept\tRaphûz asked you to join him for tea and a smoke at the Tale-warden encampment near Telperiën's Wall.\n2\tTalk to Raphûz\tYou learned much about the young man you helped. You should say your farewell in the shadow of Telperiën's Wall.\n",
[687]="70051541\n1\tTalk to Begonia Grubb\tBegonia Grubb can be found in Wistmead, by the Party Tree, and in the town centre of all housing neighbourhoods. Begonia Grubb will give you a doormat with treats if you promise to lay it out and then visit others' in a costume yourself.\n",
[688]="7002616B\n1\tCollect flowers for the Festival Garden (total: 8)\tFlowers are conveniently located outside the Festival Garden in the fields near Duillond. You should pick flowers to be replanted in the Festival Garden.\n2\tPlant flowers in the Festival Garden (total: 8)\tFlower pots are in the Festival Garden of Duillond. You should plant the flowers you collected in the flower pots.\n3\tSpeak with Forlad in the Festival Garden\tForlad is in the Festival Garden in Duillond. You should see if Forlad is satisfied with your work.\n",
[689]="70033FF8\n1\tSpeak with Cyneberg outside of Lornsettle\tCyneberg can be found outside of Lornsettle, looking out at the Isingmere. You should speak with Cyneberg.\n2\tUse the horn to call Cyneberg at the west gate\tA summoning horn for calling Cyneberg can be found at the west gate of Forlaw. You should go to the west gate when you are ready to depart and call Cyneberg to your side.\n3\tSpeak with Cyneberg at your side\tCyneberg can be found with you at the west gate in Forlaw. You may use the whistle to call her to your side if you become separated. You should speak with Cyneberg.\n4\tTalk to Cyneberg at the cross-roads in the Whitshaws\tCyneberg can be called by using your whistle. The cross-roads can be reached by following the road out of Forlaw into the Whitshaws. You should speak with Cyneberg once you reach the first cross-roads.\n5\tRide with Cyneberg to the cross-roads\030Use Whistle\tCyneberg can be called by using your whistle. The cross-roads can be reached by following the road out of Forlaw into the Whitshaws. You should speak with Cyneberg once you reach the first cross-roads.\n6\tTalk to Cyneberg at the cross-roads\tCyneberg can be called by using your whistle. The cross-roads can be reached by following the road out of Forlaw into the Whitshaws. You should speak with Cyneberg once you reach the first cross-roads.\n7\tTalk to Cyneberg at the cross-roads\tCyneberg can be found at the cross-roads in the Whitshaws. You should speak with Cyneberg.\n",
[690]="7004D06D\n1\tFind Dagrun's family crest\030Find Othur's family crest\030Talk to old Isgird\030Search the Master's safe\tThe crests and old Isgird can be found about Lake-town. The old Master's chest can be found in the Master's manor in Lake-town. You should find representations of Dagrun's and Othur's family crests, speak to old Isgird, and check the old Master's chest to verify that Othur's stolen treasure is not there.\n2\tTalk to the crowd gathered outside the Master's manor\tA crowd of people have gathered near the Master's manor in Lake-town. You should present your findings to the curious crowd of people.\n3\tCompleted\tQuelled suspicions of Dagrun's bloodline.\n",
[691]="70062E49\n1\tTalk to Murig\030Talk to Deryn\tMarget has asked you to check on her friends in Lhan Garan. Talk to Murig and Deryn.\n2\tTalk to Marget\tMarget is waiting to hear from you about how her friends are faring. Talk to Marget in Lhan Garan.\n",
[692]="70066BAD\n1\tTalk to Gladion\tGladion has invited you to join him and his family for dinner. Talk to him when you're ready to go inside.\n2\tTalk to Gladion\tSupper has concluded and Gladion has moved outside for some fresh air. Speak to Gladion in the field next to his house.\n",
[693]="70022762\n1\tCollect proof that you made it to the attic\030Collect proof that you made it to the basement\030Collect proof that you made it to the Creeping Wing\030Collect proof that you made it to the Cobwebbed Wing\tProof of your visit to every corner of the Haunted Burrow lies in each of the levels off the main floor. You should collect proof that you have visited the four main areas of the Haunted Burrow and return before the time runs out.\n2\tReturn to Poppy Cotton with the proof of your expedition\tPoppy Cotton is outside the Haunted Burrow, by the Party Tree. You should quickly return to Poppy Cotton with the proof that you bravely and skilfully walked in her footsteps inside the Haunted Burrow.\n",
[694]="700331C3\n1\tCollect spears from goblins\tSpear-wielding goblins can be found atop Khadar-zarâm. You should collect spears from the lethal goblins.\n2\tCollect spears from goblins (total: 6)\tSpear-wielding goblins can be found atop Khadar-zarâm. You should collect spears from the lethal goblins.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have taken the weapons of the spear-throwing goblins of Khadar-zarâm, making the stair safer for those who wish to leave Moria through the eastern door.\n",
[695]="70046BFF\n1\tCollect the Ranger's brooch\t\n2\tCollect the Ranger's brooch\tThe brooch can be found on the ground within Torngroth. You have discovered a worn Ranger's brooch within Torngroth and should collect it before returning to Henneth Annûn.\n3\tDeliver the brooch to the Rangers at Henneth Annûn\tHenneth Annûn can be found in north-central Ithilien. You have collected the brooch and should now return it to someone in Henneth Annûn.\n",
[696]="700284B2\n1\tDefeat the Butcher (quantity: see journal)\tThe goblin-butcher may be found somewhere in the caves of western Nan Curunír. You should dispatch the goblin-butcher for his foul crimes.\n",
[697]="7002733E\n1\tTalk to Lheu Brenin in Tûr Morva\tLheu Brenin is outside his home on the upper-most level of Tûr Morva. Arwel, delighted at meeting a dwarf, thinks you should speak with Lheu Brenin about another dwarf who passed through Tâl Methedras recently.\n2\tExamine the axe on the table near Lheu Brenin\030Examine the sword on the table near Lheu Brenin\030Examine the staff on the table by Lheu Brenin\tWeapons are arrayed on a table next to Lheu Brenin. Lheu Brenin has asked you to examine the weapons on the table next to him and to identify which of them was Lindar's gift to him.\n3\tTalk to Lheu Brenin in Tûr Morva\tLheu Brenin is outside his home on the upper-most level of Tûr Morva. You have examined the weapons and should now tell Lheu Brenin which weapon was a gift from the dwarf Lindar.\n4\tTalk to Penrod in Tûr Morva\tPenrod is among the northern buildings in Tûr Morva. Lheu Brenin has asked you to speak with his Brehur, Penrod.\n",
[698]="7002D6D9\n1\tCollect healthy mud-roots in Tharâkh Bazân (total: 10)\tTharâkh Bazân can be found to the west of Búkk's camp in Durin's Way. Búkk has asked you to look for a specific plant root which only grows near sources of fresh water. He believes it may be found among the streams of Tharâkh Bazân.\n2\tReturn to Búkk with the healthy roots\tBúkk can be found at the small encampment at the eastern edge of Tharâkh Bazân. You have collected several roots near water sources that seem to match Búkk's description of mud-roots. He awaits your return at the small encampment in Tharâkh Bazân.\n",
[699]="70007300\n1\tBring the wine-flasks back to Brethilwen\030Collect wine-flasks (total: 6)\tThere are goblins throughout Limael's Vineyard, north-west of Celondim. Brethilwen is at an old ruin overlooking the vineyard to the east. Brethilwen has asked you to recover wine flasks of a rare and ancient vintage from the goblins who stole them.\n",
[700]="7006E4CA\n1\tCollect wine-flasks (total: 12)\030Pick grape clusters from the vines (total: 6)\tYou have been asked to recover wine-flasks of a rare and ancient vintage from the goblins who stole them. While you are in Limael's Vineyard, you should pick the remaining grapes.\n2\tFind and defeat Pampraush\tYou have recovered the wine-flasks from the goblins who stole them and picked the remaining grapes. You should now confront the goblin leader, Pampraush.\n",
[701]="7004300A\n1\tSearch hiding-places inside the Hall of the Gentle Hand (total: 3)\030Search hiding-places outside the Hall of the Gentle Hand (total: 3)\tPossible hiding-places can be found both within and without the Hall of the Gentle Hand. Brunil believes someone has poisoned her medicines and she wants you to check likely hiding-places.\n2\tTalk to Brunil in the Hall of the Gentle Hand\tBrunil can be found within the Hall of the Gentle Hand, in Imloth Melui. Your search of possible hiding-places turned up nothing suspicious. You should return to Brunil and see if she is satisfied.\n",
[702]="7006EB90\n1\tBeckon the merchant Galpêsh outside the walls of Kûr Anzar\030Find the merchants of Kûr Anzar down the hill\tUse the back gate of Kûr Anzar, then find the vendors down the hill and beckon them to follow you inside.\n2\tSpeak with Numûru at the top of Kûr Anzar\tSpeak with Numûru at the top of Kûr Anzar.\n3\tSpeak with Galpêsh\030Speak with Hâdima\030Speak with Urgu\030Speak with Mulnûri\030Speak with Mâkhbur\tSpeak with five vendors at the top of Kûr Anzar and offer your aid.\n4\tClean up rubble piles for Urgu (total: 6)\030Hang posters for Mulnûri (total: 5)\tClean up rubble piles for Urgu and hang posters for Mulnûri.\n5\tSpeak with Mizâdi at the top of Kûr Anzar\tSpeak with Mizâdi at the top of Kûr Anzar.\n",
[703]="7002F892\n1\tCollect wolf-pelts from Greyhide wolves (total: 8)\tGreyhide wolves can be found along the stream of water leading to the woods, south-east of the trader's outpost. Léodrim has agreed to adjust his prices, as long as you can procure him hides from the Greyhide wolves, so that he might manufacture more goods.\n2\tReturn the Greyhide-pelts to Léodrim\tLéodrim awaits your return at the trader's outpost along the road west of Elthengels. You have secured Greyhide wolf-pelts for the trader Léodrim, so that he may lower the prices on his goods.\n",
[704]="7002C613\n1\tHelp Wynmar see Noriel one last time before his departure\tWynmar is at the hunters' camp in Thinglad. You should speak with Wynmar once more to help him with what seems to be a harmless wish: to look upon the object of his love one last time.\n2\tTalk to Ninil\tNinil is at Haldirith in Thinglad. You should speak with Ninil.\n",
})
